@codex review

Please review updated head `68946f507155def3f4967281619e14a7b9a78b61`, including fixes for discussion_r4435296877 and discussion_r4435296886. Runtime metadata now preserves prerequisite providers/aliases; special-target lookups normalize names; independent groups remain lazy when invocation context changes. Regression tests reproduce both review findings and pass after the fixes. All 21 architecture tests and 192 correctness cases pass. The new timestamp/group/provider expectations also pass against external GNU make (six test methods, including the 96-case timestamp/mode/job matrix).

Full portable/sanitizer/incremental and strict 60-cell performance qualification is pending for this head. Please check the new metadata's validation and the direct/generated behavior again; the PR remains draft.

@codex review

Please check the final display fix in `8070519`: deferred Ninja recipes retain Ninja's default progress display; explicit KATI_VERBOSE/V verbosity and silent prefixes are preserved. The two existing snapshot expectations remain unchanged. The 22 architecture tests and the four double-colon snapshot scenarios pass. Your review of `68946f5` completed without findings; both earlier provider/alias findings are fixed.

The full normal run on `68946f5` passed 26/28 groups and failed only these two output snapshots in both profiles, matching CI. That attempt is retained as failed evidence. Final-source normal/sanitizer/incremental and the unchanged 60-cell performance plan will run after the final build. No performance result is yet claimed for this review's changes.
